---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Modern Inground Pool Remodel Ideas & Design Trends | GK Swimming Pools"
  description="Pebble finishes, dark plaster, glass tile. Here are the pool remodel design trends homeowners are choosing right now and how to pick what fits your backyard."
  canonical="https://www.gkswimmingpools.com/blog/pool-remodel-design-trends"
>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BlogPosting",
    "headline": "Modern Inground Pool Remodel Ideas and Design Trends",
    "description": "Pebble finishes, dark plaster, glass tile. Here are the pool remodel design trends homeowners are choosing right now and how to pick what fits your backyard.",
    "datePublished": "2026-09-02",
    "author": { "@type": "LocalBusiness", "name": "GK Swimming Pools", "telephone": "(818) 804-8204" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "LocalBusiness", "name": "GK Swimming Pools", "url": "https://www.gkswimmingpools.com" },
    "image": "https://www.gkswimmingpools.com/images/blog/pool-remodel-design-trends-hero.webp",
    "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "https://www.gkswimmingpools.com/blog/pool-remodel-design-trends" }
  })} />

  <section class="blog-hero">
    <div class="blog-hero__bg">
      <img src="/images/blog/pool-remodel-design-trends-hero.webp"
        alt="GK Swimming Pools crew applying a dark plaster finish during a pool remodel"
        fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1400" height="769" />
    </div>
    <div class="blog-hero__overlay"></div>
    <div class="container blog-hero__inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Pool Remodeling Guide</span>
      <h1>Modern Inground Pool Remodel Ideas and Design Trends</h1>
      <div class="blog-meta">
        <span>GK Swimming Pools</span>
        <span class="blog-meta__dot"></span>
        <span>6 min read</span>
        <span class="blog-meta__dot"></span>
        <span>September 2, 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="blog-body">

        <div class="blog-intro">
          <p>If your pool is due for a remodel, it's worth thinking beyond just patching what's worn. A remodel is a chance to rethink the whole look of your pool, and a few clear trends are shaping what homeowners are choosing right now. Most of it comes down to two decisions: plaster finish and tile.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Trend One</span>
          <h2>Pebble Tec and Textured Finishes</h2>
          <p>One of the biggest shifts in pool remodeling right now is a move away from smooth, standard plaster toward pebble aggregate finishes. Pebble Tec and similar products embed small stones into the plaster surface, giving the pool floor real texture instead of a flat, uniform look.</p>
          <p>The appeal isn't just aesthetic. Pebble finishes tend to hold up longer than traditional plaster, resisting wear and staining better over time. For homeowners already remodeling, it's become a popular upgrade since it improves both the look and the durability of the pool in one step. The result is a more natural, almost lagoon-like appearance that's hard to get with standard plaster.</p>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider"/>

        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Trend Two</span>
          <h2>Plaster Color Trends</h2>
          <p>Plain white plaster used to be the default. That's changed. Here's what's trending now.</p>

          <div class="color-cards">
            <div class="color-card">
              <div class="color-card__swatch color-card__swatch--dark"></div>
              <h3>Darker Tones</h3>
              <p>Deep blue, gray, and black plaster are increasingly popular. Dark plaster makes the water itself look richer and more reflective, closer to a natural pond or lake than a typical backyard pool. In the right light, the effect is dramatic.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="color-card">
              <div class="color-card__swatch color-card__swatch--light"></div>
              <h3>Lighter, Classic Tones</h3>
              <p>White and light blue plaster still give that clean, resort-style look many homeowners want, and they tend to make smaller pools feel more open.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="color-card">
              <div class="color-card__swatch color-card__swatch--mid"></div>
              <h3>Mid-Tone Blues</h3>
              <p>A safe, versatile middle ground, offering some depth without committing to a dramatic dark finish.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>There's no universally right choice. It depends on the size of your pool, how much sun it gets, and the overall style of your backyard.</p>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider"/>

        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Trend Three</span>
          <h2>Tile Choices That Define the Look</h2>
          <p>If plaster sets the base, tile is where a remodel really gets its personality. A few options homeowners are gravitating toward:</p>

          <ul class="blog-factor-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Glass Tile</strong>
              <span>Along the waterline, glass tile adds shine and color depth that catches light differently throughout the day. It's a popular choice for pools that want a more modern, polished feel.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Natural Stone Tile</strong>
              <span>Brings a more organic, high-end look, and pairs especially well with pebble finishes for a cohesive, textured design.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Mosaic Accents</strong>
              <span>Showing up as small design details, like a border pattern or an accent panel, rather than covering the full waterline.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider"/>

        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Popular Pairings</span>
          <h2>Combinations That Are in High Demand</h2>
          <p>The trend we're seeing the most interest in isn't one single choice, it's how plaster and tile are paired together. A few combinations that come up often:</p>

          <div class="combo-list">
            <div class="combo-item">
              <div class="combo-item__num">01</div>
              <div class="combo-item__body">
                <h3>Dark Pebble Finish + Glass Mosaic Waterline</h3>
                <p>A dramatic, modern look with texture and shine working together.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="combo-item">
              <div class="combo-item__num">02</div>
              <div class="combo-item__body">
                <h3>Lighter Plaster + Natural Stone Accents</h3>
                <p>A softer, more organic combination that still feels upscale.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="combo-item">
              <div class="combo-item__num">03</div>
              <div class="combo-item__body">
                <h3>Mid-Tone Blue Plaster + Classic Ceramic Tile</h3>
                <p>A reliable, timeless option for homeowners who want an updated pool without a dramatic style shift.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="blog-divider"/>

        <div class="blog-section">
          <span class="eyebrow">Making the Choice</span>
          <h2>Choosing What's Right for Your Pool</h2>
          <p>The best combination depends on your outdoor space, how much sun and shade the pool gets, your home's overall style, and how you actually use the pool day to day. A finish that looks great in photos isn't always the right practical choice for every yard.</p>

          <div class="blog-tip">
            <div class="blog-tip__label">See It In Person</div>
            <p>The most reliable way to figure out what fits is seeing plaster and tile samples in person, ideally against your actual pool. Colors read very differently under direct LA sun than they do on a showroom shelf or a website photo.</p>
          </div>

          <p>GK Swimming Pools handles pool remodels throughout the San Fernando Valley and Santa Clarita area, and we can walk you through plaster and tile options directly so you can see how they'll actually look before committing.</p>

          <div class="blog-cta-inline">
            <a href="/remodel-quote" class="btn btn--primary">Get a Free Estimate</a>
            <a href="tel:8188048204" class="btn btn--outline">(818) 804-8204</a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Ready to Redesign Your Pool?</h2>
      <p>Free on-site estimate. See plaster and tile samples against your actual pool. Serving Santa Clarita and the San Fernando Valley.</p>
      <a href="/remodel-quote" class="btn btn--primary">Get My Free Estimate</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</Layout>

<style>
  .blog-hero { position:relative; height:460px; overflow:hidden; display:flex; align-items:flex-end; }
  .blog-hero__bg { position:absolute; inset:0; }
  .blog-hero__bg img { width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; object-position:center 45%; display:block; }
  .blog-hero__overlay { position:absolute; inset:0; background:linear-gradient(to top, rgba(6,47,97,.90) 0%, rgba(6,47,97,.35) 60%, rgba(6,47,97,.12) 100%); }
  .blog-hero__inner { position:relative; z-index:2; padding-bottom: var(--space-12); }
  .blog-hero__inner .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .blog-hero__inner h1 { color:var(--color-white); font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3.6vw,2.6rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width:820px; }
  .blog-meta { display:flex; align-items:center; gap: var(--space-3); color:rgba(255,255,255,.72); font-size:var(--text-sm); font-weight:600; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  .blog-meta__dot { width:4px; height:4px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--color-aqua); }

  .blog-body { max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; }
  .blog-intro { background:var(--color-mist); border-left:4px solid var(--color-aqua); padding:var(--space-6) var(--space-8); margin-bottom:var(--space-12); border-radius:0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0; }
  .blog-intro p { font-size:var(--text-lg); color:var(--color-deep); font-weight:600; line-height:1.7; margin:0; }
  .blog-section { margin-bottom:var(--space-12); }
  .blog-section .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .blog-section h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .blog-section p { color:var(--color-muted); line-height:1.85; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .blog-divider { border:none; border-top:2px solid var(--color-border); margin:var(--space-12) 0; }

  /* COLOR CARDS */
  .color-cards { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:var(--space-4); margin:var(--space-6) 0; }
  .color-card { background:var(--color-white); border:1.5px solid var(--color-border); border-radius:var(--radius-sm); overflow:hidden; }
  .color-card__swatch { height:70px; width:100%; }
  .color-card__swatch--dark { background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0d1b2a 0%,#1b3a5c 100%); }
  .color-card__swatch--light { background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e8f4f8 0%,#b8dce8 100%); }
  .color-card__swatch--mid { background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2d6a9f 0%,#4a9bc4 100%); }
  .color-card h3 { font-family:var(--font-heading); font-weight:700; font-size:var(--text-sm); color:var(--color-deep); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; margin:var(--space-5) var(--space-5) var(--space-3); }
  .color-card p { font-size:var(--text-sm); color:var(--color-muted); line-height:1.7; margin:0 var(--space-5) var(--space-5); }

  /* FACTOR LIST */
  .blog-factor-list { list-style:none; margin: var(--space-6) 0; }
  .blog-factor-list li { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap: var(--space-1); padding: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-5) var(--space-6); border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border); position:relative; }
  .blog-factor-list li::before { content:""; position:absolute; left:0; top:var(--space-6); width:8px; height:8px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--color-aqua); }
  .blog-factor-list strong { font-family:var(--font-heading); font-weight:700; font-size:var(--text-base); color:var(--color-deep); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.03em; }
  .blog-factor-list span { font-size:var(--text-sm); color:var(--color-muted); line-height:1.75; }

  /* COMBO LIST */
  .combo-list { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:var(--space-4); margin:var(--space-6) 0; }
  .combo-item { display:flex; gap:var(--space-5); align-items:flex-start; background:var(--color-white); border:1.5px solid var(--color-border); border-left:3px solid var(--color-aqua); border-radius:var(--radius-sm); padding:var(--space-6); }
  .combo-item__num { font-family:var(--font-heading); font-weight:800; font-size:1.5rem; color:var(--color-aqua); line-height:1; flex-shrink:0; }
  .combo-item__body h3 { font-family:var(--font-heading); font-weight:700; font-size:var(--text-base); color:var(--color-deep); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.03em; margin-bottom:var(--space-2); }
  .combo-item__body p { font-size:var(--text-sm); color:var(--color-muted); line-height:1.7; margin:0; }

  .blog-tip { background:var(--color-deep); border-radius:var(--radius-sm); padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8); margin: var(--space-8) 0; }
  .blog-tip__label { font-size:var(--text-xs); font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.15em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--color-aqua); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); font-family:var(--font-heading); }
  .blog-tip p { color:rgba(255,255,255,.88); margin:0; }

  .blog-cta-inline { display:flex; gap: var(--space-4); flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .btn--outline { display:inline-block; border:2px solid var(--color-deep); color:var(--color-deep); font-family:var(--font-heading); font-weight:700; font-size:var(--text-sm); letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8); border-radius:var(--radius-sm); text-decoration:none; }

  @media (max-width:900px) { .color-cards { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  @media (max-width:640px) {
    .blog-hero { height:360px; }
    .blog-intro { padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5); }
    .combo-item { flex-direction:column; gap:var(--space-3); }
    .blog-cta-inline { flex-direction:column; }
  }
</style>
